WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.860
5 Years Ago

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:07.300
Mars Orbit

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.250
If he hadn't been an old scholar...

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.000
who had already retired from the Academy...

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.240
Mars Orbit

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.820
it probably wouldn't have caught his interest.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.690
A small, nameless comet that sprouted a tail...

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.820
for the first time in a thousand years...

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.290
Inside of it, there she was.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.690
She had lost her memories and had been asleep for who knows how long.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.960
There was only one wish that she could recall.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.540
That was...

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.310
No... no... ri... ri...

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:12.470
...ko...

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.630
Groovin' magic
Groovin' magic

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:23.020
yorisoeba itsudemo
Whenever we're close to each other

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:29.660
kitsuku musunda kutsuhimo ga mune wo kyun to saseru
My firmly tied shoelaces make my heart twinge

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:52.050
se no takai anata ga mioroshite iru no yo
You're looking down on me from your tall height

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:57.010
sotto kami wo naderu furi wo shite
I quietly pretend to stroke my hair

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.320
chikadzuite ki wo hikitai no
hoping to get closer and catch your eye

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.520
"dou shita no?" tte jirasanaide
"What's the matter?" Don't give me that

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:13.980
koi no countdown junbei wa itsudemo OK
Countdown to love, I'm ready anytime

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.720
3, 2, 1, futari wa...
3, 2, 1, we're...

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.670
Groovin' magic
Groovin' magic

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.660
soda sui ni tokeru
Soluble in soda water

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:29.080
amaku setsunai koi no iro mune no kyun to saseru
The bittersweet color of love makes my heart twinge

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:52.660
Space Force, Chief of Staff, 3rd Grand Fleet

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:54.030
Some records remain of the fact...

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.300
that a black hole weapon was used in the outer Sol System...

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.790
in order to intercept the hundreds of millions of fluctuating gravity wells...

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.490
that were coming to invade our planet.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.850
That is the black hole we now know as Exelio...

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.450
the so-called Nest Hole of the space monsters.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:13.550
After the counter-offensive operation in which mankind invested everything it had...

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.080
it is hypothesized that...

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:19.350
a Sol System Absolute Defense System consisting of unmanned Buster Machines was built.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.060
At the same time, it seems that...

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.990
the fluctuating gravity wells' remaining forces had survived...

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.180
and most of all, mankind was probably feeling worn out.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:33.310
They chose to seal away warp technology and shut themselves off within the Sol System.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.580
The defense system evolved over time to become stronger and more efficient.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.110
Ironically, as a result...

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:47.580
the system wound up heavily resembling our enemy, the fluctuating gravity wells.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.080
Their current form is what we now refer to as space monsters.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:53.410
Commander, 3rd Grand Fleet, Admiral Dhorasoo

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.090
The defense system was...

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.380
built to protect us, mankind, wasn't it?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.060
It seems that after a certain point, the system sensed the same threat from us...

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:07.680
the people they were supposed to protect, as they sensed from the fluctuating gravity wells.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.060
That was...

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.020
...the Topless.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.510
Mover of Planets
Episode 5

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:22.690
I don't know how good the meals at the Fraternity were...

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.350
but I'd like you to get used to ours already.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.570
All of your companions are also receiving treatment under military control.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.100
Though...

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.650
it shouldn't pose any problem in this facility as long as you wear that corrective gear...

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.980
no matter how horrible a disease being Topless may be.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:48.620
Sol System, New 10th Planet

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.540
After the Titan incident...

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:50.840
the world completely changed for us.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.340
Kaminatsuki

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.650
In the face of a real space monster, the fluctuating gravity well...

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.860
the power of the Topless didn't mean a thing.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.660
Topless powers are no longer the force that will save mankind.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.450
Being Topless means...

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:08.490
having abnormal activity in the frontal lobes of the brain,

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.200
Surgeon General

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.660
peculiar to younger age groups.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.210
But it's possible to rehabilitate those afflicted, if we treat it in its early stages.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:16.520
Welfare Department Deputy Director

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.750
Legislation regarding medication...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.040
as well as surgical treatment, is well under way.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:20.080
As of the day before yesterday...

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.540
Military Police Vice-Secretary

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.300
the revocation of the treaty has been put into effect.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:27.140
The forced expropriation of the Fraternity has also been taken care of.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:31.280
With all of this done, we plan to enter into peace negotiations with the space monsters.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.350
We're actually rather lucky...

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:38.350
After all, we were able to welcome Buster Machine #7.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.970
Wow, you made it here.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.380
I'm sorry for taking so long to visit!

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.960
Sorry! Ah, I'm so sorry!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.830
I thought I should at least bring something Onee-sama likes...

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:04.210
With all of these physicals and psychological tests and things going on...

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.660
I couldn't get them to let me go.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.800
Wow, how'd you manage to get these in such a remote area?

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.260
If I say I want something...

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.730
the nice men in the secret service find a way to get it for me.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.310
Last night's dinner was Peking duck and foie gras!

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.120
I think I could even go to Earth.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.270
After all, we agreed to go to your house and look for skylarks, right, Onee-sama?

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.400
WOW!

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.740
May I have this skylark?

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.170
...it's not a skylark, it's a crane.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.290
Princess, you're so awkward!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:40.810
On Earth, you give it to someone as a way of showing that you hope they stay well.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:43.290
It's really supposed to be the one visiting who brings it.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.860
Wow, Onee-sama, you really are amazing!

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.990
Hey, nice helmet.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:12.750
Yo!

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.160
You're looking pretty chipper.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.170
Y'know, I grew scared way back when.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.340
I submitted the report of my expiration before I actually found it...

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.870
and stepped down from <i>Dix-Neuf</i>.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.790
If you never know for sure, you never lose hope, right?

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.180
Well, that's how I used to look at it, anyway.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:38.180
So, now I'm a repair subcontractor for the Buster Machine Public Corp.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.600
It's nothing to fret over.

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:55.660
The left arm was artificial to start with...

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.240
and the horn piercing through it is even older.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.420
According to the public corp's records, it's a battle scar at least 500 years old.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:05.320
Why don't they repair it?

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.190
<i>Dix-Neuf</i> apparently didn't want them to.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:09.680
It's embedded in part of the brain stem.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.840
Because of that, there are several Exotic Maneuvers he can't use.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:17.670
Even so, he risks losing his entire reservoir of priceless battle experience...

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:19.160
if it's treated the wrong way.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.690
To make up for the short-lived Topless...

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.270
he builds up experience over the ages.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.000
That's what their artificial intelligence is for...

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.840
What's that?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.190
The scrawlings of previous pilots.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:36.550
This area has armor dating back to before the sixth overhaul, so...

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:38.570
it's probably from a senior pilot dating back 40 generations or so.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.580
"Sixteen-day-old moon. Into silent night I walk, setting out alone."

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.960
"He makes no move; I go, leaving him behind."

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.650
You can read it?

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:51.020
Unrequited love... Something that never changes over the ages.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:55.860
All he has left is battle experience. We're all just left by the wayside and forgotten.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:57.450
How's Nicola?

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.010
He says the slight fever won't go down.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.230
Who's that over there?!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.790
Er, uh... I'm terribly sorry!

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:16.880
New ol' man, you've been told not to enter without permission, right?

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.800
Oh, dear... I'm terribly sorry about this, really.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:22.700
My apologies, I mean, err, this is so embarrassing... I'm sorry!

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.380
Wh-What?

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.150
She said she really wants you to teach her how to do these.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.130
Why not go to her?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.880
You are her Onee-sama, after all.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.510
Onee-sama?

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:41.760
Onee-sama! ...Hm?

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:45.770
'Sup.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:55.640
I'm afraid of setting out on my own.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:59.160
So, y'know, I want a little going-away present.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.400
You'll give me one, won't you?

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:02.850
I want everything you have...

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.700
You're a Buster Machine in the flesh, aren't you?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.710
That means you're an eternal Topless, doesn't it?

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:27.850
Someone!

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.110
Nono!

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.310
Onee-sama!

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.830
Why not me?

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:50.290
You always looked so tough and full of confidence...

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.430
I knew you were only pretending to be kind, but even still, I liked you!

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:58.630
Why is it that now that you've reached your
expiration, you can't even look at me?!

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.470
It's because I was Topless that I wound up this way!

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.800
What the hell do Buster Machines matter to grown-ups?!

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.610
What the hell do Candians matter?! It's all so dumb!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.610
Umm... Onee-sama...

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.610
Don't follow me!

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.610
I'm not your Onee-sama!

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:31.870
Far North Fleet (Space Force 3rd Grand Fleet)

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.210
Flagship <i>Karakoram</i>

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.580
This is a display showing when the abnormality first appeared.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.240
Combat Information Center

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.510
This is from 12 minutes ago.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.180
An immense number of space monsters...

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.640
have begun gathering together.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.950
The space monsters' Nest Hole is a region shrouded in mystery...

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.430
an area in which mankind has never before set foot.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.660
In particular, the inside of the accretion disc cannot be discerned...

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.860
via X-ray or gravitational wave scanning.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:55.870
The only way to ascertain what may be inside is to go in there directly.

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:58.950
Extrapolating from the similarities between this and the Titan incident...

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.590
Is it about to invade the Sol System again?

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.870
The new fluctuating gravity well?!

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.940
They'll come back, won't they?

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:24.700
Yeah...

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.580
Two days later...

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.430
Nono and I were on the fleet headed for the space monsters' Nest Hole.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:39.060
Everyone was expecting great things of Nono.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:43.610
Buster Machine #7 would be able to save mankind, they hoped.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.080
If so... then there's no need for me.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.750
Former 13th Planet in the Sol System, Jupiter 2

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:05.840
It is not a planet in its current state.
Having lost 90% of its mass, only its core remains.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:21.440
No one knows the reason for it, but...

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.450
...the birds on Mars died out.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:32.230
Have you heard the story of the last bird on Mars?

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:37.790
By the time she hatched from her egg, she was already the last of her kind.

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.580
She never flew in the sky.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:46.910
She kept standing by the water's edge, never once even trying to fly.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:48.720
But...

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:51.940
One day, when she grew up...

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:54.670
on the night of a meteor shower...

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.850
she flew away.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:00.270
It was almost as though she was trying to chase the falling stars...

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.910
Maybe she set out to travel the world of the stars.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:06.320
Abandoning Mars, where she was born and raised.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:18.660
That was the last record of her.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:33.770
Ammonia-type space monsters confirmed.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.920
Space monsters deployed ahead, 75,000 in number.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.440
That number is still increasing.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:40.920
80,000.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:43.560
85,000.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.570
Are you sure they're not going to attack us?

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:46.830
It's a defense force to protect their nest.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:47.800
90,000.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.330
It's a defense force to protect their nest.

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:50.950
95,000.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.550
They've most likely come to welcome Buster Machine #7.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:55.040
They've topped 100,000.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:55.830
Number 7!

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:17.850
Behold, all of these space monsters are obeying #7 alone.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:21.190
An amazing spectacle even to a Topless like you, isn't it?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:24.540
She is truly the queen of the space monsters.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.710
The one who wanted you brought along was #7, you know.

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:30.940
I'll bet it was so that you could witness this display of power.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.350
New 11th Planet in the Sol System

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:01.690
Black Hole Exelio

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:24.240
Reverse gravitational fluctuation confirmed near the outer edge of the ergo region...

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.460
where the space monsters are gathering.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.380
The scale is incomparable to that of the Titan incident!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.880
This is a fluctuating gravity well?!

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:35.350
It's crawling up out of a black hole?!

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:40.940
The space monsters must have been keeping this gravity well sealed away...

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:43.270
ever since it got trapped in Exelio...

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:45.220
in order to protect mankind.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:47.320
However...

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:54.990
It looks like it's about to break out!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.240
Buster Machine #7 is moving in!

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:16.840
She's sealing the cracks with micro black holes?!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:21.290
She's rewriting the surrounding physical space, and forming a degeneracy generator...

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.890
It's technology that we've lost now.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.190
She'll save us with power from the age of myths...

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.250
Queen of the space monsters?

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.160
No, she is truly the goddess of the Sol System!

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:37.510
Number... 7...

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.490
All right, send the fleet forward!

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.120
We'll support her with the Graviton Cannon!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.080
Between our fleet, the strongest in the Space Force, and #7...

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.250
we have nothing to fear!

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.710
Non-combatant personnel, if you could leave the bridge?

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:52.300
You'll get in the way.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.340
Enter Level 1 Combat Alert!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.610
Ready the main gravity cannon via Code 4!

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.710
Bow Graviton Cannon, fire!!

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:25.490
What the?!

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:27.080
It warped space?!

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.210
Abnormal increase in gravitational fluctuations!

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:31.440
It's rising up to the visible wavelength spectrum!

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:32.750
That's impossible!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:35.880
It's overflowing!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:05.310
The diameter of the fluctuation is over 12,000 kilometers!

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.750
12,000 kilometers?!

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:09.170
You're saying it's bigger than the Earth?!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.820
Its full body hasn't appeared yet, either.

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.000
#7 is using a beam attack!

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:22.450
Even #7's beam?!

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:27.770
Onee-sama!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.480
Admiral! Order all hands to abandon ship!

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.110
We're evacuating as well!

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:42.080
Code 9, all hands are ordered to abandon ship!

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:46.860
We've got room for one more! Hurry up, this is the last escape pod!

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:50.300
From #25 to #21...

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:52.740
Wait...

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:15.460
Even Nicola wound up that way...

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.230
The twins, everyone, they all died...

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:23.690
My hands are shaking...

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:26.150
How pathetic...

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:36.200
Ever since the time we first met on Mars,
the space monsters were searching for Nono.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:42.420
They were trying to bring their own master home.

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:45.480
Nono's amazing.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.100
Nothing at all like me...

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.550
It was that way from the start...

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:05.720
I, Nono, wanted to become like you, Onee-sama.

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:10.190
I was always so jealous of you, Onee-sama. Because...

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:14.040
you and Nono-Riri are a lot alike.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:21.550
The person called "Nono-Riri" wasn't anybody special...

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.070
She was just an ordinary girl.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:33.980
She's shaking?

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:41.940
It's not that the world has changed.

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:44.500
It's not that Nono has changed.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:46.900
The one who's changed...

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.040
is me.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:58.040
Let's fly, Onee-sama!

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:05.630
<i>Dix-Neuf</i>!!

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.110
12 ships remaining, including ours.

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:17.890
The flagship's IFF signal has been lost!

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:21.860
The space monsters' defense forces are being driven back...

00:22:22.120 --> 00:22:25.200
Is even #7 no match for it?

00:22:34.900 --> 00:22:37.830
Admiral, have the fleet pull back. I'll handle it.

00:22:38.110 --> 00:22:40.340
You're the Topless from earlier?

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:44.580
I'm going to hit it with Jupiter 2. Retreat back beyond the shockwave perimeter!

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:46.090
What are you saying?!

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:48.550
That's a feat beyond any human capability!

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:54.560
I can do it. If I'm with Nono, I can do anything!

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:02.520
EXOTIC MANEUVER!!

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:13.950
Jupiter 2, Remaining Core

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:42.400
The Topless can move even the planets?!

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:21.030
Direct hit at 20 kilometers a second!

00:24:21.030 --> 00:24:22.030
My God!

00:24:33.690 --> 00:24:34.660
That's...

00:24:34.660 --> 00:24:37.990
It didn't come out of the Black Hole Exelio...

00:24:38.330 --> 00:24:40.790
It absorbed Exelio itself!

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:44.040
Freely manipulating black holes...

00:24:44.040 --> 00:24:46.820
not dying even after being slammed with Jupiter 2...

00:24:46.820 --> 00:24:48.520
Mankind's natural enemy...

00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:51.670
Ether-separating wave detected!

00:24:51.670 --> 00:24:55.160
We believe the fluctuating gravity well will warp from this region!

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:58.100
300 until it reaches the warp-entry critical point!

00:24:59.580 --> 00:25:03.600
If we don't take it down now, mankind will be wiped out.

00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:07.110
Gather the remaining ships.

00:25:07.390 --> 00:25:09.440
We'll at least get in one good shot...

00:25:10.180 --> 00:25:11.410
It won't do anything, most likely.

00:25:13.940 --> 00:25:16.660
However, #7 would...

00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:27.330
Nono, you understand?

00:25:28.240 --> 00:25:32.050
The only chance we have to take it down is now, before it warps.

00:25:32.050 --> 00:25:35.340
We need an even greater energy than that of a planetary impact.

00:25:35.660 --> 00:25:39.020
#7 will advance into the remaining core of Jupiter 2.

00:25:39.550 --> 00:25:43.920
By igniting a series of micro black holes, she can trigger a degeneracy chain.

00:25:44.320 --> 00:25:47.350
Turning Jupiter 2 into a black hole?

00:25:47.570 --> 00:25:50.350
If there were an ultra gravitational collapse at such close range...

00:25:50.730 --> 00:25:53.320
it should be able to destroy even the fluctuating gravity well.

00:25:56.940 --> 00:25:59.030
You mean to send her off on a kamikaze attack?

00:25:59.630 --> 00:26:03.330
I won't let you go alone, of course. I'll come too.

00:26:03.630 --> 00:26:06.590
I'm getting goosebumps. The two of us, saving the world together!

00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:10.290
Let's become stars together, Nono!

00:26:22.750 --> 00:26:24.140
What's wrong, Nono?

00:26:30.390 --> 00:26:30.940
Nono?

00:26:41.740 --> 00:26:42.660
Nono...

00:26:44.830 --> 00:26:45.940
Moon Surface, Lunar Tokyo: The Imperial City

00:26:45.940 --> 00:26:48.060
Buster Machine #7...

00:26:48.060 --> 00:26:49.120
has rejected the plan and flown off?

00:26:49.120 --> 00:26:51.160
Space Force Privy Staff Council

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:53.560
The fact that she's abandoned us means that...

00:26:53.560 --> 00:26:54.870
we can safely assume...

00:26:54.870 --> 00:26:57.220
the defense system is also gone.

00:26:57.440 --> 00:27:02.720
Henceforth, we'll have no choice but to fight off the fluctuating gravity well...

00:27:02.720 --> 00:27:04.100
with our own power.

00:27:04.680 --> 00:27:07.020
But that's for the best.

00:27:07.460 --> 00:27:10.830
This could be considered a rite of passage...

00:27:11.920 --> 00:27:14.610
for mankind to truly reach adulthood.

00:27:15.110 --> 00:27:18.540
But still, to flee before the enemy like that...

00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:22.620
Reaching warp critical point in 1.5... 1.2...

00:27:22.620 --> 00:27:27.010
Admiral, the fluctuating gravity well is entering warp.

00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:47.810
Nono...

00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:52.750
NONO!!!

00:27:56.140 --> 00:27:59.150
...NONO!!!

00:27:59.150 --> 00:28:02.660
To Be Continued

00:29:14.270 --> 00:29:17.860
May this feeling reach that person...
douka konna omoi ga

00:29:17.860 --> 00:29:22.520
And the world, and the universe
ano hito ni sekai ni uchuu ni made

00:29:22.520 --> 00:29:30.260
Another one spills down
todokimasu you ni tomata hitotsu koboreochiru

00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:40.110
Bye-bye, stardust tears
bye bye hoshikuzu namida

00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:51.810
Next Episode Preview

00:29:52.060 --> 00:29:57.690
Onee-sama... do you know what she, who never once tried to fly despite having wings...

00:29:58.090 --> 00:30:01.280
found in the meteor shower?

00:30:01.940 --> 00:30:05.160
Next time, on Gunbuster 2!, the final episode:

00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:05.770
The Story of Your Life
Final Episode

00:30:05.770 --> 00:30:08.040
The Story of Your Life.

00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:08.830
The Story of Your Life
Final Episode

00:30:08.870 --> 00:30:12.130
Don't Miss Out!
